# GPU policy (userland/gpu-policy, docs/gpu-hybrid-plan.md): which API a process tries, in order.
#   PATTERN  API...      PATTERN = fnmatch glob on the process name, or ext:GLOB on NSExtensionPointIdentifier.
#   API = metal | gl | cpu. The first matching line wins; the owner's /var/db/negronigpu/policy and
#   BUNDLE/gpu-policy.local are read before this staged file. No match: "metal gl cpu".
# Only a FAILED API (dead-man strikes at the limit, GPU lost, a failure record of this boot) is skipped for the
# next one. A DISABLED API (off file, not in clients, boot-arg, memory rule) keeps today's meaning.
# Off: /var/db/negronigpu/off, BUNDLE/gpu-policy.off or NEGRONIGPU=0.

# Render server: Metal (YUV/XR surfaces, 41 pipelines); GL (CA's OGL renderer on Mesa) when Metal failed.
backboardd                       metal gl cpu
# In-process Metal users with no GL path in iOS 16 (RenderBox, VFX, CAMetalLayer posters, MPS, VectorKit, ANGLE-Metal):
# a GL context would not be used, so the fallback is the CPU path of the framework.
SpringBoard                      metal cpu
chronod                          metal cpu
*Poster                          metal cpu
*PosterExtension                 metal cpu
*PosterProvider                  metal cpu
ext:com.apple.widgetkit-extension metal cpu
com.apple.MapKit.SnapshotService metal cpu
com.apple.WebKit.GPU             metal cpu
# Everything else: EAGLContext users (GLKit, games, CoreImage-on-GL) get GL from NegroniGL.bundle as before.
*                                metal gl cpu
